  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "管理學",
    "sub_ename": "MANAGEMENT",
    "describe_ch": "本課程之目的是希望使學生：(一)對現代「學習型組織」之運作環境、運作方式、社會與道德考量等具有初步之認識；(二)結合組織行為學中對領導、激勵、溝通等理論以期建立學生對組織管理具備初步之能力。本課程為以建立管理思維為主的基礎學科，課程實施將側重於理論介紹與課堂討論。期中期末考以筆試方式進行以確保學生能吸收所學。",
    "describe_eh": "The purpose of the \"Industrial Organization & Management\" course is two folds: (1) to introduce the operation environment, operation principles, as well as the social/ethic considerations of modern learning organizations to students; (2) to introduce how leaderships, motivation, and communications are going to work in a learning organization so that the students are able to apply proper managerial techniques in the future. This course is designed as an fundamental class to establish students managerial sense. Lectures as well as in-class discussions are selected as the major teaching approaches while paper-based exams are given as the evaluation tools.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "本課程之目的是希望使學生：(一)對現代「學習型組織」之運作環境、運作方式、社會與道德考量等具有初步之認識；(二)結合組織行為學中對領導、激勵、溝通等理論以期建立學生對組織管理具備初步之能力。本課程為以建立管理思維為主的基礎學科，課程實施將結合理論與實務，結合多元之上課方式以確保學生學習效果。",
      "describe_en": "The purpose of this course is to enable students to: (1) Have a preliminary understanding of the operating environment, operating methods, social and moral considerations of modern \"learning organizations\"; (2) Combine leadership, motivation, and communication in organizational behavior And other theories in order to establish students' initial ability of organization and management. This course is a basic subject focusing on the establishment of management thinking. The implementation of the co"
    }
